From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Keyan <vincent.keyan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:41:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] shader_split: Snowdrop's chained LZ4 entries in SDF version
 23 slices

Starlink: Battle for Atlas keeps its NVN shaders in SDF slices with a BERG
version 23 header, which have none of the compressed records that Sparks
of Hope's and Kingdom Battle's slices have. The split found no shaders,
and the build stopped there.

Each entry is a stream of LZ4 sequences in 64 KB pieces. Its matches may
reach back into the entries before it in the same block, and a piece's
last match may run past the piece's end, where it is cut. The part lists
the game ships beside its slices (_DataPartList.txt) give the entries'
places. The shader objects are the 'mcache' assets and the shader
package cache in their blocks, with the section layout snowdrop_shaders
already reads (now snowdrop_sections). An update rewrites whole slices,
and the extracted base folder holds the rewritten copies too, so a slice
index's entries come from the newest list naming it.

An entry must use exactly its stored bytes, and only a last match may be
cut, so a list that does not match its slice is a [RED] line for that
slice. Starlink v393216: 19,373 unique shaders (16,060 vertex, 2,947
pixel, 366 compute), all translated for iOS; zero before.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Starlink: Battle for Atlas's shaders were not found (the shader split had no reader for SDF version 23's chained LZ4 entries)
Issue: none yet (Starlink: Battle for Atlas bring-up)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
